From: virtudude <virtudude@protonmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm: let a socket lease holder yield to drm-lease-v1 clients

A socket lease holder started with --drm-lease-yield is suspended when a
drm-lease-v1 client requests the lease and resumed when that client
releases it. Suspend reuses the VT-switch path: the holder stops
presenting, parks its page flip reader so the shared event queue is left
to the new client, and acks only once nothing of its can commit; the
broker grants only on that ack and otherwise leaves it the holder. Resume
forces a modeset. A holder that did not opt in keeps the exclusive
semantics. The flip handler also ignores events whose user data is not
one of its own, since every holder reads from a dup of the same lease.
